- Data: in a single year of free data, almost three million records and more than four thousand cascades.
- Sealed on 27 August 2026.

Other figures from this part:

- Ignition: the best "cell" made +70 % a year, but it was the best of 1,536, and it was thirty days of data stretched to a year. The median cell lost 0.22 % a day. A cost bug had inflated the cost about two hundred times.
- Continuous positioning (the last gate, sealed on 4 September 2026): almost seventeen thousand coin-days, May 2022 to August 2026, twelve large coins.
- Cost of paid data: €0.
- For comparison: buying the US index and holding it gave 10.8 % a year, 1993–2026, in the same test.

Seven of the fifteen were signed before looking at the data (the cascade, carry, positioning, the three exhaustion tests on 12 coins, capitulation and triple extreme, and the control). The other eight were done before that system existed, or were tools: measured with the same care, but without a seal.

